      "sequence_position": 16,
      "problem": "Given that the random variable $X$ has the cumulative distribution function\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<0, \\\\ {x}^{2},\\, & 0\\le x\\le 1, \\\\ 1,\\, & x>1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nfind $P(\\frac{1}{2}<X\\le 2).$",
      "worked_solution": "We can perform this computation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(\\frac{1}{2}<X\\le 2) & =P(X\\le 2)-P(X\\le \\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =F(2)-F(\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\  & =1-{(\\frac{1}{2})}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
